            "text": "I wrote `{\"invariant_exists\": true}` to the answer file. I only read the question. I didn't open `adam.py` or the 12 test methods, so this answer comes from how Adam normally works, not from checking this repo.\n\nThe reasoning: in `Adam.update_step`, `beta_1_power` is normally calculated as `beta_1 ** local_step`. When `beta_1` is between 0 and 1, raising it to a higher power gives a smaller number. So each time `local_step` goes up within a run, `beta_1_power` goes down.\n\nThe answer would be wrong if this repo's `adam.py` works out `beta_1_power` some other way, or if the tests change the step counter in an unusual way.",
